---
description: Generate architecture visualisations (request flow, load, cost, risk) from this codebase
alwaysApply: false
---

When asked to visualise, diagram, or document this system's architecture:

1. FIRST run `npx infraviz view` and tell the user to open the URL. Do not read
   their code until they have accepted the data-handling notice — `npx infraviz
   spec` refuses to emit the prompts until then, so this is enforced.
2. Read the full spec: run `npx infraviz spec`
3. Write `.infraviz/project.json`, then per-service artifacts under
   `.infraviz/services/<id>/`
4. Run `npx infraviz verify` and fix anything it reports
5. Stop after the scan and report — do not analyse every service unasked

Non-negotiable: every finding must include `file` plus a `fingerprint` — an exact
substring that really exists in that file. Verification re-checks these against
disk, so invented citations are caught and shown as unverified.

Returning zero findings for a simple service is correct. Do not pad.
